=== PE 892: Zebra Irrationals ===

Zebra numbers have alternating digit parity (odd/even).

=== Asymptotic growth ===
Count_d = 9 × 5^{d-1} for d ≥ 1
  d=1: count=9 = 9
  d=2: count=9×5 = 45
  d=3: count=9×5×5 = 225
  d=4: count=9×5×5×5 = 1125
  d=5: count=9×5×5×5×5 = 5625
  d=6: count=9×5×5×5×5×5 = 28125

=== Zebra continued fractions ===
A zebra continued fraction has terms that alternate
between two sets, e.g., a0, b1, a2, b3, a4, b5,...
This generalizes simple continued fractions.

PE answer: 469137427
